## 2. Administrator Setup: Project Creation, APIs & Guardrails

Run the following commands as a GCP Organization / Project Administrator (requires `roles/resourcemanager.projectCreator` and `roles/billing.user`):

### Step 0: Set Administrator Environment Variables
Export configuration variables once in your terminal session before running provisioning steps:

```bash
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Workshop Administrator Environment Variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
export BILLING_ACCOUNT_ID="{{ config.billing_account_id }}"
export ORG_DOMAIN="{{ email_domain }}"
export TEAM_COUNT={{ config.team_count }}
export PROJECT_PREFIX="{{ config.project_prefix }}"
export PROJECT_ID="{{ first_project_id }}"   # Default single-project target for individual operations
{% if config.folder_id -%}
export FOLDER_FLAG="--folder={{ config.folder_id }}"
{% else -%}
# export FOLDER_FLAG="--folder=<FOLDER_ID>"   # Uncomment if required by {{ config.organization }} Org Policy
{% endif -%}
```

### Step 1: Create Projects & Link Billing
```bash
for N in $(seq 1 "${TEAM_COUNT:-{{ config.team_count }}}"); do
  NN=$(printf "%02d" "${N}")
  PROJECT_ID="{{ bash_project_id }}"
  echo ">>> Creating project ${PROJECT_ID}..."
  gcloud projects create "${PROJECT_ID}" \
    --name="{{ config.organization }} AGY Team ${NN}" \
    ${FOLDER_FLAG:-}

  echo ">>> Linking billing account to ${PROJECT_ID}..."
  gcloud billing projects link "${PROJECT_ID}" \
    --billing-account="${BILLING_ACCOUNT_ID:-{{ config.billing_account_id }}}"
done
```

### Step 2: Enable Required APIs
Enable {% if config.auth_mode == "vertex_paygo" %}Vertex AI, {% endif %}Service Usage, Resource Manager, Gemini for Google Cloud{% if config.enable_cloud_resources %}, and workload deployment{% endif %} APIs:

```bash
for N in $(seq 1 "${TEAM_COUNT:-{{ config.team_count }}}"); do
  NN=$(printf "%02d" "${N}")
  PROJECT_ID="{{ bash_project_id }}"
  echo ">>> Enabling APIs on ${PROJECT_ID}..."
  gcloud services enable \
{% if config.auth_mode == "vertex_paygo" %}    aiplatform.googleapis.com \
{% endif %}    serviceusage.googleapis.com \
    cloudresourcemanager.googleapis.com \
    cloudaicompanion.googleapis.com \
    billingbudgets.googleapis.com \
    orgpolicy.googleapis.com{% if config.enable_cloud_resources %} \
    run.googleapis.com \
    artifactregistry.googleapis.com \
    cloudbuild.googleapis.com \
    storage.googleapis.com{% endif %} \
    --project="${PROJECT_ID}"
done
```

> **Note:** Enable only public Google Cloud service APIs (`aiplatform.googleapis.com` and `cloudaicompanion.googleapis.com`). Do not enable private or deprecated internal endpoints.

### Step 3: Quota & Spend Guardrails

#### A. Budget Alert Cap (Recommended Primary Guardrail)
{% if config.auth_mode == "vertex_paygo" -%}
Gemini 2.5 and Gemini 3.x models on Vertex AI utilize **Dynamic Shared Quota (DSQ)** on the `global` endpoint, where overall traffic allocation is dynamically managed. Set a Cloud Billing budget alert per team project to monitor spend:
{% else -%}
Set a Cloud Billing budget alert per team project to monitor cloud workload and API spend:
{% endif %}

```bash
# Create a budget alert per team project (e.g. ${{ config.budget_alert_usd }} threshold)
for N in $(seq 1 "${TEAM_COUNT:-{{ config.team_count }}}"); do
  NN=$(printf "%02d" "${N}")
  PROJECT_ID="{{ bash_project_id }}"
  gcloud billing budgets create \
    --billing-account="${BILLING_ACCOUNT_ID:-{{ config.billing_account_id }}}" \
    --billing-project="${PROJECT_ID}" \
    --display-name="Budget - {{ config.organization }} Workshop Team ${N}" \
    --filter-projects="projects/${PROJECT_ID}" \
    --budget-amount={{ config.budget_alert_usd }}USD \
    --threshold-rule=percent=0.5 \
    --threshold-rule=percent=0.8 \
    --threshold-rule=percent=1.0 \
    --threshold-rule=percent=1.0,basis=forecasted-spend
done
```

{% if config.auth_mode == "vertex_paygo" -%}
#### B. Consumer Rate Limit Overrides (Secondary Guardrail)
To place rate limits on standard Vertex AI endpoints:

1. **Regional Aggregate Online Prediction Cap:**
   ```bash
   for N in $(seq 1 "${TEAM_COUNT:-{{ config.team_count }}}"); do
     NN=$(printf "%02d" "${N}")
     PROJECT_ID="{{ bash_project_id }}"
     gcloud alpha services quota create \
       --service=aiplatform.googleapis.com \
       --consumer="projects/${PROJECT_ID}" \
       --metric="aiplatform.googleapis.com/online_prediction_requests" \
       --unit="1/min/{project}/{region}" \
       --dimensions=region={{ config.compute_region }} \
       --value={{ config.rate_limit_rpm }} \
       --force
   done
   ```
2. **Per-Model Global Inference Cap:**
   Overrides for `global_generate_content_requests_per_minute_per_project_per_base_model` can be applied via the Cloud Console:
   * Navigate to **IAM & Admin ➔ Quotas & System Limits**.
   * Filter Service: `Vertex AI API` ➔ Metric: `global_generate_content_requests`.
   * Select the target base model and submit the consumer quota override (e.g., {{ config.rate_limit_rpm }} RPM).
{% endif %}

#### C. Restrict Allowed Models

By default, all Vertex AI foundation models are accessible. **If you would like to restrict the models available to workshop attendees**, execute the script below to apply Google Cloud's Organization Policy constraint (`constraints/vertexai.allowedModels`). If you do not wish to enforce model restrictions, you can safely skip this step.

This example configuration allowlists frontier reasoning and high-throughput workhorse models configured for Antigravity workflows:
* **Google Models:** `Gemini 4 Argon` and `Gemini 3.8 Flash`
* **Anthropic Partner Models:** `Claude Opus 5.5` and `Claude Sonnet 5.5`

```bash
# Create the allowed models policy definition
cat << 'EOF' > /tmp/allowed_models_policy.yaml
name: projects/${PROJECT_ID}/policies/vertexai.allowedModels
spec:
  rules:
  - values:
      allowedValues:
{% for model in config.allowed_models %}      - {{ model }}
{% endfor %}EOF

# Enforce the allowed models constraint across all {{ config.team_count }} team projects
for N in $(seq 1 "${TEAM_COUNT:-{{ config.team_count }}}"); do
  NN=$(printf "%02d" "${N}")
  PROJECT_ID="{{ bash_project_id }}"
  echo ">>> Setting allowed models policy on ${PROJECT_ID}..."
  sed "s/\${PROJECT_ID}/${PROJECT_ID}/g" /tmp/allowed_models_policy.yaml > "/tmp/policy_${PROJECT_ID}.yaml"
  gcloud org-policies set-policy "/tmp/policy_${PROJECT_ID}.yaml" \
    --billing-project="${PROJECT_ID}"
done
```

> **Permission Prerequisite:** Applying organization policies via `gcloud org-policies set-policy` requires `roles/orgpolicy.policyAdmin` (Organization Policy Administrator) on the target project, folder, or organization.
>
> **Gemini Enterprise Subscriptions:** In subscription environments, partner models (such as Claude) can also be toggled centrally via the Google Cloud Console under **Gemini Enterprise ➔ Settings ➔ AI developer tools**.

