## 3. Administrator Setup: IAM Roles & Team Permissions

Grant team members the required roles on their team's project.

### Role Requirements per Attendee

| Permission Need | Role Name | Role Identifier | Purpose |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
{% if config.auth_mode == "vertex_paygo" -%}
| **Model Inference** | Vertex AI User | `roles/aiplatform.user` | Invokes Gemini models on Vertex AI (`aiplatform.endpoints.predict`). |
| **Project Billing / Quota** | Service Usage Consumer | `roles/serviceusage.serviceUsageConsumer` | Authorizes API consumption and bills usage to the project. |
{% else -%}
| **Gemini Enterprise Access** | Gemini for Google Cloud User | `roles/cloudaicompanion.user` | Authorizes subscription-backed Gemini Enterprise assistance in the project. |
| **Project Billing / Quota** | Service Usage Consumer | `roles/serviceusage.serviceUsageConsumer` | Authorizes API consumption and project service checks. |
{% endif -%}
{% if config.enable_cloud_resources -%}
| **Resource Creation** | Project Editor | `roles/editor` | Builds and deploys services (Cloud Run, Cloud Storage, Artifact Registry, Cloud Build). |
{% endif %}
{% if config.auth_mode == "gemini_enterprise" %}
> **Subscription Seat Assignment:** Ensure each attendee or team Google Group (`{{ first_group_email }}` .. `{{ last_group_email }}`) has an active **Gemini Enterprise** license seat assigned via Google Admin Console or the Google Cloud Gemini Admin panel.
{% endif -%}
{% if config.enable_cloud_resources %}
> **Least-Privilege Alternative:** If security policy restricts granting `roles/editor`, administrators can grant the following scoped roles instead:
> * `roles/run.admin` (Cloud Run management)
> * `roles/iam.serviceAccountUser` (Mandatory: authorizes Cloud Run to run as the Compute service account)
> * `roles/cloudbuild.builds.editor` (Mandatory for deploying Cloud Run services from source)
> * `roles/storage.admin` (Cloud Storage buckets & objects)
> * `roles/artifactregistry.admin` (Container images)
> * `roles/logging.viewer` (Build and service log inspection)
{% endif %}

### Step 4: Team Google Groups & IAM Permissions

#### Option A: Team Google Groups (Recommended for Teams)

##### 1. Automated Group Creation via CLI (Optional)
If your administrator account holds **Groups Admin** privileges in Google Workspace or Cloud Identity (`roles/cloudidentity.groupsAdmin`), you can automatically provision all {{ config.team_count }} team Google Groups:

```bash
# Set your Cloud Identity domain or Organization ID (e.g. {{ email_domain }})
ORG_DOMAIN="${ORG_DOMAIN:-{{ email_domain }}}"

for N in $(seq 1 "${TEAM_COUNT:-{{ config.team_count }}}"); do
  NN=$(printf "%02d" "${N}")
  GROUP_EMAIL="{{ bash_group_email }}"
  echo ">>> Creating team group ${GROUP_EMAIL}..."
  gcloud identity groups create "${GROUP_EMAIL}" \
    --organization="${ORG_DOMAIN}" \
    --display-name="{{ config.organization }} Workshop Team ${N}" \
    --description="Antigravity workshop attendee group for Team ${N}"
done
```

> **Manual Alternative:** If your account lacks Cloud Identity organization permissions, request your Workspace administrator create these groups in the [Google Workspace Admin Console](https://admin.google.com) (**Directory ➔ Groups ➔ Create group**).

##### 2. Bind Project IAM Roles to Team Groups
Once the groups exist, bind the necessary roles across all {{ config.team_count }} team projects:

```bash
for N in $(seq 1 "${TEAM_COUNT:-{{ config.team_count }}}"); do
  NN=$(printf "%02d" "${N}")
  PROJECT_ID="{{ bash_project_id }}"
  GROUP_EMAIL="{{ bash_group_email }}"

{% if config.auth_mode == "vertex_paygo" %}  gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding "${PROJECT_ID}" \
    --member="group:${GROUP_EMAIL}" \
    --role="roles/aiplatform.user"
{% else %}  gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding "${PROJECT_ID}" \
    --member="group:${GROUP_EMAIL}" \
    --role="roles/cloudaicompanion.user"
{% endif %}
  gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding "${PROJECT_ID}" \
    --member="group:${GROUP_EMAIL}" \
    --role="roles/serviceusage.serviceUsageConsumer"
{% if config.enable_cloud_resources %}
  gcloud projects add-iam-policy-binding "${PROJECT_ID}" \
    --member="group:${GROUP_EMAIL}" \
    --role="roles/editor"
{% endif %}done
```

#### Option B: Individual Attendee Grants (Direct User Binding)

```bash
