## 4. Attendee Setup: Antigravity Client Sign-In

Attendees must connect Antigravity to their assigned team project using the {% if config.auth_mode == "vertex_paygo" %}Pay-As-You-Go{% else %}Subscription (Gemini Enterprise){% endif %} option.

### Method A: Antigravity Desktop App & IDE Extensions (VS Code, JetBrains, Zed)

```
Settings ➔ Account ➔ Sign In ➔ Use business account ➔ Continue with Google Cloud
```

1. Open **Settings ➔ Account** in Antigravity (or IDE extension) and click **Sign In**.
2. Click **“Use business account”**.  
   *(Do **NOT** click "Continue with Google" — that invokes consumer login).*
3. Click **“Continue with Google Cloud”** and authenticate with your corporate Google credentials in your browser.
4. On the **Select Billing Model** screen:
{% if config.auth_mode == "vertex_paygo" %}   * Select **“Pay As You Go”** (*"Pay only for the tokens you use, billed through Gemini platform"*).
   * *(Do **NOT** select "Subscription" — no seat licenses are assigned).*
{% else %}   * Select **“Subscription”** (*Gemini Enterprise seat license*).
{% endif %}5. On the **Provide Google Cloud Project** screen:
   * Enter your assigned team project ID: `{{ project_placeholder }}`.
   * Click **Next**.
6. On the **Choose Region** screen:
   * Select **`{{ config.region | capitalize }}`** and click **Next**.  
   > [!IMPORTANT]
   > You **MUST** select **`Global`**. Do **NOT** select `United States` or `Europe`. Antigravity's Gemini models are served from `locations/global`; regional selections will return HTTP 404 errors.
7. Accept the **Terms of Service & Data Use** and click **“Get started”**.

*(Note for older Antigravity clients v1.4.x: If prompted for Project ID before Billing Model, enter `{{ project_placeholder }}`, select `Global`, and choose `{% if config.auth_mode == "vertex_paygo" %}Agent Platform - Pay as you go{% else %}Gemini Enterprise - Subscription{% endif %}` on the fallback screen).*

---

